  "security_implications": "This block controls key writes (en_key_write, clr_keyidx) and valid signaling (kmac_valid) to the SHA3 engine, directly touching secret material. The lc_escalate_en_i override does not clear en_key_write or kmac_valid when forcing st_d to StTerminalError, so a concurrent StKey state can propagate a key write and data valid in the same cycle as the escalation, potentially leaking key material. The sparse_fsm_error_o alert is not raised immediately on escalation unless the error counter is already saturated, delaying or suppressing the security alert. The terminal error state itself suppresses the alert for the first 99 cycles, creating a window where a transient error or reset can hide the fault.",
